      "writtenOn": "2026-10-18T15:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SPDM supports two verification paths: certificate-based verification and pre-provisioned raw-public-key verification. Redfish represents these using Certificate and PublicKey(https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/ComponentIntegrity.v1_3_2.json). As per the spec, PublicKey may be included only when SlotId \u003d\u003d 15 (0xF) and the requester was pre-provisioned with the responder’s public key. The verifier needs to rely on the signed measurement transcript to select the verification method.\n\n@florian.sorin@arm.com I don\u0027t see an impact for verifier whether it is null or empty. If this is intended to align with the spec, I think a comment can be added in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88828 to address the issue.",
